Unite Next

This project is a modified fork of Unite Shell by the hardpixel/unite-shell
contributors: https://github.com/hardpixel/unite-shell
The verified upstream source is commit
7a67cecf52a543c3620a3859b909cc81e9204894.

Modification notice — 2026-10-29
Unite Next changes include GNOME Shell 50/51 modernization, lifecycle and
resource ownership fixes, native preferences, build and verification tools, and
an independent installation and settings identity. These modifications do not
imply endorsement by the upstream project or the projects credited below.

Modification notice — 2026-10-30
System tray hosting and its settings were removed. Notification positioning,
GTK application styling and XWayland decoration handling remain supported.
Subsequent corrections isolate control-theme CSS, unify control eligibility,
restore native notification sizing, refresh selected user themes and define
primary-monitor precedence with safe GTK styling behavior.
Accessible window-action translations follow the GNOME Shell 51.0 and GTK
4.24.0 language catalogs, retaining their contributors' credit:
https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnome-shell/-/tree/51.0/po
https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gtk/-/tree/4.24.0/po

Modification notice — 2026-11-02
GTK stylesheet updates retain displaced files for recovery from concurrent
edits, and imported paths are escaped. Window effects follow maximization and
primary-monitor changes; open preferences track theme availability. Regression
and native desktop scenarios cover these transitions and resource cleanup.

The project retains the GNU General Public License version 3 in LICENSE.
Existing source copyright notices and translator credits remain applicable.
Translation authors and language teams are credited in translations/*.po in the
corresponding sources.

